603 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Every home tells a story\204you just have to slow down enough to notice it. That\220s why this first step is all about observation. Once a month, take a calm, intentional walk around the outside of your home. No tools, no stress\204just you noticing what\220s changed.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

604 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Pay attention to things like discoloration on siding, shifting soil, damp spots, sagging trim, or cracks along the foundation. These small signs often appear long before something breaks. Think of it like learning your home\220s language\204eventually, you\220ll spot what doesn\220t belong without even trying.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

605 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(And once something catches your eye, it\220s time to move in closer and check whether it\220s worth fixing\204or just worth noting.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[6]>>
