671 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Most homeowners don\220t notice something\220s wrong until water shows up or wood starts to shift\204and that\220s especially true if you bought your home quickly, like so many people did during the rush of recent years. You weren\220t handed a manual, and no one walked you through what to watch for outside. That\220s not your fault\204but now you have a chance to pay attention before the damage demands your attention.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

672 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(You don\220t need to know exactly what\220s wrong. You just need to trust your instincts\204when something doesn\220t look or feel right, that\220s enough. Flag it, tag it in your notes, and keep moving. That simple act means you\220ve done your part for now\204and you\220ll be ready if and when it needs a professional\220s attention.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

